  "type": "Album",
  "description": "Watchout! is the fourth studio album and fifth album overall by Martha and the Vandellas, released on the Gordy (Motown) label in 1966. The album included the top 10 hit singles, \"I'm Ready for Love\" and \"Jimmy Mack\" and the ballad single, \"What Am I Gonna Do Without Your Love?\". This was one of the last albums by the group with songs by Holland–Dozier–Holland who, the following year, left Motown, and with William \"Mickey\" Stevenson. The album became the group's highest charting studio album at number 116, reaching the peak on January 11, 1967, staying on the charts for eight weeks.",
